3. The brief facts of the present case are that on 18.02.2002 at about 06:45pm, the Food Officials consisting of Ms Usha Kiran and Sh. Ram Pratap Singh, Food Inspectors under the supervision of Local Health Authority/SDM Sh. R.K. Chauhan and his staff members reached at M/s Mubin Store,
Main Road, Babu Nagar, Mustafabad, Delhi, where he was found running the business of CA no.
8627/2016 Munabbar Khan Vs. Food Inspector Pages 2 of 10 various food articles, including Red Chilli Powder which was lying stored/exposed in sealed polypacks of Red Chillies Powder ( Ready for sale in the packing of 1 kilogram each ), bearing no label declaration for sale for human consumption ;
- that FI disclosed his identity and expressed his intention to purchase a sample of Red Chilli Powder from the vendor, to which he agreed and the price of the commodity was paid to him ;
- that thereafter as per the prescribed procedure under the PFA Act and Rules after giving notice to the vendor and offered towards sale price of sample to which he agreed, sample was then lifted ;
- that sample was separately packed, fastened, marked and sealed and necessary documents were prepared at the spot in the presence of appellant/accused including Notice as per Form-VI, and panchnama proceedings etc ; that thereafter one counterpart of sample was sent to Public Analyst (PA) in intact condition and other two counterparts were deposited with SDM/LHA ;
- that vide report dated 07.03.2002, the PA found the sample to be not conforming to the standards of Red Chilli Powder because it was coloured with un-permitted synthetic colouring matter and is also misbranded as there was violation of Rule 32 (a)(d)(e)&(f).
- that upon receipt of report, SDM/LHA directed investigation which was carried out by FI and after completion of investigation sanction under Section 20 of the PFA Act was obtained from the Director PFA.
